WEBVTT

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.230
Hey, you're back.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.250
S-Sorry.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:18.530
Little Wing
Orphanage

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.460
I know what you said, but I...

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.660
It's not like it's your fault.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.530
You don't need to apologize.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:24.330
Besides, I'm sure the girls will be more 
satisfied if they give it their best shot.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.360
All right, I'm headed to work.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.990
Hey, what do you do for work?

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.190
I'm an exorcist.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.310
<i>Have you forgotten something, Master?</i>

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.090
No, it's me, Kyo.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.150
Welcome, Kyo-nii.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.610
Hey, morni—

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.030
I'm in the middle of a bath.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.830
Give me a moment.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.750
Hey, Sora!

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.760
You need to dry off!

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:14.880
Kyo!

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.100
Look out!

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.430
That was close.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.030
S-Sorry.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.460
Please and thank you.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.270
Please and thank you.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.780
U-Um...

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.510
Um...

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:31.890
U-Um...

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.660
Want to take a short break?

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.150
Fureai Park

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.410
We haven't given out too many flyers yet.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.150
I guess it's not as easy as you'd think.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.390
Yum.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.250
Seriously...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.500
It really is good, though.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.810
Okay, let's get back to work.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.570
Good night.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.690
Sora!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.860
I did say "Let's take a short break," 
but we have to get back to work.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.900
Just five more minutes.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.410
Onii-chan's surrounded 
by girls other than me!

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.930
He's letting another girl sleep on his lap!

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.060
Bursting Scent of Arrest!

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.570
Cure Police!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.620
Class President?

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.490
Class President?

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:19.210
Wait, are you all in Kurumi's class?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.450
So, Onii-cha—

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.840
Nii-san, what might you be doing?

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.840
Nii-san?

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.430
That's what I always call you, isn't it,

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.520
Nii-san?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.230
Sure, sure, absolutely.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:43.860
So, what might you be doing at a place like 
this, with my classmates, on a weekend?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.670
Uh...

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.820
Well, these three...

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.620
U-Um...

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.830
I'm sorry.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:02.540
Kyo-san was playing with us.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.050
I never knew he was your brother, Nukui-san.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.670
Playing with you?

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.110
O-Oh, really?

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.310
That's nothing to apologize for.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:23.060
Okay, Nii-san, I have to 
go to my piano lesson.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.940
Have fun with them, you hear?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.200
Okay, stop.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:36.810
What's going on?

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.500
You don't seem to have any focus.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.980
Sorry.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.090
Hi, please and thank you.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.380
Please and thank you.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.470
U-Um...

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.190
Let's try again tomorrow.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.410
T-Tomorrow is...

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.270
Do you have plans for tomorrow?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:11.630
Our class decided to have a meet up so we 
could get to know each other better.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:17.530
W-We're going to be 
hanging out at Izumi Park,

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.920
that way we can become closer friends soon.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.170
Who cares about that?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.420
We decided we don't need to go if 
we have plans to go out with family.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.300
Let's deliver flyers tomorrow, too.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:35.560
But I think you should go 
to those kinds of events.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.850
Master said so, too.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.560
That's all the more reason to.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:52.950
U-Um, maybe not tomorrow, 
but would you come the next day?

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.820
Sure, of course.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.680
I'm home.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.550
Career Card
Manga Artist
Salary: $20,000

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.420
So...

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:12.830
What's this about?

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.470
Just shut up and play with me.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.300
Uh... right.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:21.060
Also, as a special rule, 
you aren't allowed to get married.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:31.940
"Just keep setting foot 
again until you can't.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.940
<b>Prose Poetry</b>

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.950
Even though I fear loss whenever 
every time I meet someone,

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.700
I want to live the best I can, 
color life with emotion,

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.980
and howl at the beauty of the world."

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.220
That's well-written.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.460
Nukui, you might have talent.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.720
Next, Kaneda.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.800
Yes, sir.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.340
"I had a dream yesterday.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.750
A dream of a sleepless night.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:07.530
I couldn't sleep, even in my own dream.
It was a depressing dream.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:13.070
In my dream, I couldn't sleep,
so I wanted to hurry and wake up."

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.070
Cool poem, bro.
 lolol

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.420
It was hilarious.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.510
Morning.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.030
He's coming.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>Class Duty
Nemoto,
Nukui the poet</b>

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>Howl for me!! lol</b>

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.750
Attendance

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.150
Let's see...

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.750
Who's on class duty today?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.970
Nukui-kun the poet.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.600
I wonder if he came up with that 
thing yesterday by himself.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.350
Did he?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.910
That was hilarious.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.100
You should do it, too.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.850
Oh, come on. Stop.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.310
Nukui?

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.690
You're finally awake.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.580
When are you getting up?

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.680
G-Good morning.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.680
Don't "good morning" me.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.390
It's not really even morning.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.180
You stayed up all night again, didn't you?

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.210
By the way, Kurumi-san,
did you need something?

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.750
I-I'm going out today.

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.630
You're hanging out with your 
classmates, weren't you?

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.720
Did the girls tell you?

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:48.980
<i>It's warm.</i>

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.130
Is it a lunch box?

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:56.140
I-I had sides left over after I made my own.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:59.780
So I made some for you, too. That's all.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.170
So it is a lunch box.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.450
See you, I'm leaving now.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:08.580
Kurumi.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.080
Wh-What?

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.080
Thanks.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.840
I'm going now!

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:22.700
I guess if I'm going to make a phrase 
that can be played on a guitar,

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.050
it'd be something like this...

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:35.670
I've never arranged for a band before. 
It's pretty challenging.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.570
<i>It's still early for lunch, but...</i>

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.090
Chopsticks.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.390
Isn't this...

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.820
Wait up.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.590
You hit it too hard.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:09.220
No fires

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:09.220
Beware Gropers

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:06.650
Hey, over here.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.220
All right.

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.220
Can I see it?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.570
<i>There she is.</i>

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.660
Over here!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.640
There!

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.460
One more time!

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.480
<i>I probably shouldn't call 
to her out in the open.</i>

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:33.660
Let's play together.

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.520
Hey, Kurumi.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.500
Who cares about them?

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:45.040
They were like that in fourth grade, too.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.260
Talking to them doesn't do any good.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:56.290
Aren't they going to play together?

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:00.010
That's him, Officer.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:01.650
N-No!

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:02.520
I was just...

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.760
Toriumi-san?

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.730
Wh-Why are you here?

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.210
That's my question.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.540
Of course.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:26.250
I just happened to pass by.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:27.540
I'm leaving now.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.260
Try not to do anything 
weird when you're outside.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.440
Okay.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.440
S-Stalker!

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.050
I-I'm not.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:48.450
I just came to bring your lunch.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.950
Time to eat.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.740
It's good.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:01.830
But...

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:10.420
I wonder if it would taste 
even better together.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.070
Massage.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:24.120
Uh...

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:26.100
Why?

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:29.820
Because I'm tired from running 
around at the park, obviously.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.550
Oh, yeah?

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.210
I guess it's tough being the class president.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:36.330
I-I guess.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.440
Hey, Kurumi.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:48.220
In your class, um...

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:50.380
Is there any bullying—

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.590
Of course not.

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.020
I'd never allow bullying. 
I'm the class president.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:58.060
Everyone in my class gets along.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:04.730
But those three are kind of difficult.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.180
Difficult?

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.650
Those three are always by themselves.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.580
They don't try to play with the other kids.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:14.700
They don't really approach the rest of us.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:17.590
What about Nozomi-san?

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:21.370
Isn't she friendly enough to talk to?

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.040
Momijidani-san? Friendly?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.290
I've hardly ever seen her talk.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.910
We didn't hand out that many today, either.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.800
But today's the last day of the long weekend.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.040
We have to work hard.

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:52.440
W-Working hard is great, 
but maybe we should take a break.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.210
I'm hungry, actually.

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:58.910
Want to have donuts again?

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.710
I'm out of spending money.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.580
I know where we can go, then.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.080
Where?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:13.700
You'd better be happy, because I'm going 
to fill your belly with delicious food.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.470
For free, too.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:19.970
Our famous bread!!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:17.950
We're here.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:19.170
Here?

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:19.970
Yes.

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.220
A bakery?

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.250
Come on, this way.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.490
I'll call.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.160
Hello?

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:45.660
Um, I...

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.480
Thanks for waiting.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.890
Toriumi-san?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.100
We're back again.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.260
Sorry to disturb you at work.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:14.340
Hey, Saku-chan, this person is Kyo-san.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.630
I know.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.820
What's your relationship with her?

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.370
You know about Saku-nee, Kyo-nii?

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:25.950
Yeah.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.750
We're acquaintances, I guess.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:32.400
Saku-chan is our sister.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:34.880
We live together at Little Wing.

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:36.500
Together?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:43.760
Get over here!

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.550
Don't tell anyone.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.440
Don't you dare tell anyone!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.530
It's good.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.030
I know, right?

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:11.330
Saku-chan asks the people at the store 
to let her have some of the flawed ones.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:15.580
Speaking of which, what were 
you talking about with Sakura?

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:22.590
You remember how I transferred right after 
the beginning of first-year in middle school?

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:26.650
I've been living at Little Wing since then.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.310
I've always been in an 
orphanage since I was little,

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:33.730
but things happened, and they would shut down.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:40.240
Oh, no, it's not really that depressing.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:43.580
At least, I don't think it is.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:50.030
The old orphanage was nice, 
and I like living at Little Wing.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:52.800
Master's a dork, but he's nice.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.080
My sisters are adorable.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:59.230
But people always make 
assumptions and get on my case.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:03.050
They'd give me pity or they'd give me 
a hard time, because I'm different.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:08.720
I just wanted to be normal, but the people around me wouldn't let me.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:16.400
Then, when I switched schools, I saw it as 
an opportunity, so I started hiding things.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:20.820
I roughed up my uniform a little, so that 
I'd look like I'd been having some fun.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.150
I put on some armor.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:25.210
I got some nasty comments because of it,

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.450
and I was scolded by my teacher for it,

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.380
but it worked really well.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:35.290
I'm certain that no one pitied me during 
my three years in middle school.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:40.170
I don't really like dressing 
up like that, though.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:45.300
Wait, that doesn't mean I like 
dressing up like this, either.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.180
I just chose to work here 
because the pay is good.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.400
Secret grown-up talk?

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.110
I-It's nothing like that.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.440
Little Wing
Orphanage

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:01.440
See you.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:10.490
W-We have school starting tomorrow.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:16.460
Can we hand out flyers after school?

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:18.510
Yeah.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.380
See you tomorrow, then.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:30.890
<b>The Boy on Hiatus Descends and Flees, 
and the Girls From the Church</b>

00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:07.710
You walked the girls home for me.

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:22.420
Want to come in for a bit?

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:41.000
<b>#04 The World Is but Rock n' Roll</b>

00:23:26.370 --> 00:23:27.550
Dear Father,

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:31.720
I'm sorry for all of the trouble that
happened at the beginning of this episode...

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:35.820
Hey, wait, is this something 
I need to repent for?

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:36.900
Hey!

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:37.920
It is.

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:39.850
Why?!
